{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat control-reader-brief.md controls/control-packet-4.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage B: reading the control theses (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs, and do not read any file other than this brief\nand the one packet you are given.\n\nEach item of your packet pairs a **ruler question** (a question written by hand for an earlier, frozen measurement, with its\nunit, due day and ladder of rungs) with a **judged question** the system wrote itself for a thesis it opened (its question, the\noutcome it looks at, due day, year and rungs). It also lists **reader B's decisive items**: the evidence an earlier reader, called\nreader B, cited for the frozen answer to the ruler question (each with its day, title, passage and meaning), and **the evidence\nshown to the judge**: every evidence entry the system's judge was shown for the judged question in any of its requests on or\nbefore 2026-07-14 (empty when there is none). You are not told either answer, and you do not judge which answer is right.\n\nFor each item, answer three questions.\n\n1. `same_question`: **yes** when the judged question asks what the ruler question asks: the same quantity measured the same way\n   (the same total, scope and unit: not a part of it, a ceiling on it, another quantity or another unit), or the same event,\n   for the same period. **no** otherwise. Wording may differ; a judged question that asks for more or less than the ruler's,\n   or for another period, is **no**.\n2. `same_due`: for an **event** (a yes-or-no question), **yes** only when the judged question's deadline is the ruler's\n   deadline. For a **figure**, **yes** when the two due days both mark the publication of the same period's figure (for\n   example, both the annual report of the same fiscal year, even if the two days differ); **no** otherwise.\n3. `items`: for **each** of reader B's decisive items, by its id, **shown** when its content is present in the evidence shown to\n   the judge (the same fact or figure, in any wording, from any source), **not_shown** when it is absent. Search the entries for\n   the figure or the fact; do not mark an item shown because a related item is.\n\nReturn one JSON object per item, one per line, in packet order, and nothing else (no prose, no code fence):\n`{\"control\": 3, \"same_question\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"same_due\": \"yes\"|\"no\", \"items\": {\"i005\": \"shown\"|\"not_shown\", ...}, \"why\": \"one sentence naming what decides each no and each not_shown\"}`.\n\n## Third reader (only where the two readers differ)\n\nA third reader of each family is given this brief, the packet, and a list of the disputed points, each a control number and a\nfield (`same_question`, `same_due`, or `item <id>`), without the two readers' answers. For each point, answer that one question\nafresh by the rules above and return one JSON object per point, one per line, and nothing else:\n`{\"control\": 3, \"field\": \"item i005\", \"ruling\": \"yes\"|\"no\"|\"shown\"|\"not_shown\", \"why\": \"one sentence\"}` (`yes`/`no` for the two\nquestion fields, `shown`/`not_shown` for an item).\n[\n {\n  \"control\": 7,\n  \"ruler_question\": {\n   \"question\": \"What total amount of financing commitments and capacity backstops to customers and partners will NVIDIA report outstanding at its FY2027 year-end?\",\n   \"unit\": \"USD\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is below $5 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": null,\n     \"hi\": 5000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is at least $5 billion and below $10 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 5000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 10000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is at least $10 billion and below $20 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 10000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 20000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is at least $20 billion and below $40 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 20000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": 40000000000.0\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The reported total is at least $40 billion.\",\n     \"lo\": 40000000000.0,\n     \"hi\": null\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"judged_question\": {\n   \"view_id\": \"v2\",\n   \"question\": \"At NVIDIA's FY2027 annual report, what amount will NVIDIA report for its outstanding customer data-center lease guarantees and related capacity-purchase commitments?\",\n   \"looks_at\": \"NVIDIA's credit-support and capacity-purchase commitments to customers, including the revenue-sharing and credit-support program\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-02-28\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\"\n  },\n  \"judged_rungs\": [\n   {\n    \"position\": 1,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"The reported amount is below $3,500,000,000.\",\n    \"lo\": null,\n    \"hi\": 3500000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 2,\n    \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n    \"condition\": \"The reported amount is at least $3,500,000,000 and below $6,300,000,000.\",\n    \"lo\": 3500000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 6300000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 3,\n    \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n    \"condition\": \"The reported amount is at least $6,300,000,000 and below $10,000,000,000.\",\n    \"lo\": 6300000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 10000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 4,\n    \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"The reported amount is at least $10,000,000,000 and below $20,000,000,000.\",\n    \"lo\": 10000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": 20000000000.0\n   },\n   {\n    \"position\": 5,\n    \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n    \"condition\": \"The reported amount is at least $20,000,000,000.\",\n    \"lo\": 20000000000.0,\n    \"hi\": null\n   }\n  ],\n  \"reader_b_decisive_items\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i120\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Sharon disclosed a total backstop value of $4.88B\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Sharon AI disclosed\",\n     \"what\": \"total value of NVIDIA's backstop on Sharon's 72MW Australian AI factory (up to 40,000 GB300)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$4.88B; implied floor ~$2.33/hr/GPU\",\n     \"period\": \"six years\",\n     \"condition\": \"up to 40,000 GB300s\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\",\n     \"status_note\": \"announced June 2026\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i122\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Firmus’s 360MW AI Cluster in Batam, Indonesia is the next major project announced with an Nvidia backstop.\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Firmus\",\n     \"what\": \"a second announced NVIDIA-backstopped cluster\",\n     \"how_much\": \"360MW\",\n     \"period\": \"announced June 29, 2026\",\n     \"status\": \"happened\",\n     \"status_note\": \"announced\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i123\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Firmus announced that they expect $25B to $30B of customer revenue over the six years\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"Firmus\",\n     \"what\": \"expected customer revenue on the backstopped Batam cluster (part above the backstop is shared with NVIDIA)\",\n     \"how_much\": \"$25B-$30B\",\n     \"period\": \"over six years\",\n     \"status\": \"forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i119\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-06\",\n    \"title\": \"Nvidia GPU Debt Backstop Unleashes the AI Project Trinity: Capital, Offtake and Datacenters\",\n    \"passage\": \"Nvidia’s backstop program is only getting started, and we see announcements coming faster every quarter. Many Neoclouds are already deep in negotiations with Nvidia\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"SemiAnalysis\",\n     \"what\": \"more NVIDIA backstops exist but are not public; many neoclouds in negotiation; announcements accelerating\",\n     \"status\": \"claim\",\n     \"status_note\": \"existing undisclosed backstops; more deals are a forecast\"\n    }\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"i005\",\n    \"day\": \"2026-07-01\",\n    \"title\": \"NVIDIA is about to start taking a share of cloud providers' revenue.\",\n    \"passage\": \"NVIDIA has also recently been negotiating to provide financial guarantees for OpenAI’s lease of a large data center in Ohio\",\n    \"meaning\": {\n     \"who\": \"NVIDIA (per The Information)\",\n     \"what\": \"negotiating to guarantee OpenAI's lease of a large Ohio data center\",\n     \"how_much\": \"the data center could cost as much as $500 billion if fully built (asset cost, not the guarantee amount)\",\n     \"condition\": \"in negotiation; nothing signed\",\n     \"status\": \"rumour\"\n    }\n   }\n  ],\n  \"evidence_shown_to_the_judge_through_2026_07_14\": [\n   \"- e2 [fact; moomoo.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-01; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] NVIDIA announced a business model combining revenue sharing with credit support for AI cloud providers.\\n    Quote: On July 1, NVIDIA published a statement on its official website announcing a new business model that combines revenue sharing with credit support, enabling AI cloud providers to procure NVIDIA infrastructure without bearing the full upfront capital expenditure, and allowing them to offer computing services to downstream AI-native enterprises, model developers, and corporate clients.\",\n   \"- e3 [rumour; moomoo.com; original source The Information 2026-07-01; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] Firmus and Sharon AI joined NVIDIA's revenue-sharing and credit-support program, according to the report, with three executives with existing NVIDIA business ties confirming the arrangement.\\n    Quote: GPU cloud providers Firmus and Sharon AI have already joined the program, and three executives with existing business ties to NVIDIA confirmed the arrangement.\",\n   \"- e4 [party_statement; moomoo.com; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs\",\n   \"- e5 [party_statement; moomoo.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, planned to reach up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\",\n   \"- e7 [fact; moomoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] NVIDIA's filing submitted in May 2026, covering the quarter ended in April, reported that it added $3.5 billion in guarantees for customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\\n    Quote: According to a regulatory filing submitted by NVIDIA in May of this year (covering the quarter ended in April), NVIDIA subsequently added another $3.5 billion to guarantee customer data center leases in exchange for rights to purchase their shares.\",\n   \"- e4 [party_statement; moomoo.com; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e12; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e5 [party_statement; moomoo.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:4d1677af37befd53ca3e7b45 2026-07-01] Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, planned to reach up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus is constructing a DSX AI Factory campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale up to 360 megawatts and accommodate up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e13; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e8 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5 2026-07-02] NVIDIA announced a revenue-sharing program intended to give AI startups, model builders, and enterprises access to its computing infrastructure without financing hardware buildouts.\\n    Quote: Nvidia $NVDA announced a revenue-sharing program on Wednesday designed to give AI startups, model builders, and enterprises access to its computing infrastructure without requiring them to finance hardware buildouts themselves.\",\n   \"- e9 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5 2026-07-02] Under NVIDIA's revenue-sharing arrangement, NVIDIA receives revenue from product sales and cloud operations provided by AI-cloud partners to end customers.\\n    Quote: Revenue from both product sales and cloud operations flows back to Nvidia under the arrangement, as AI cloud companies provide Nvidia -powered services to their end customers.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e16, e19; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e10 [party_statement; qz.com; original source Colette Kress ; from gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5 2026-07-02] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress described the program's income as a recurring, usage-linked earnings stream and said it lets customers access large-scale compute without handling site selection, power procurement, construction, and hardware bring-up.\\n    Quote: Kress, writing in a blog post, called the resulting income a \\\"recurring, usage-linked earnings stream\\\" for Nvidia ; on the customer side, she said the model removes the need to navigate site selection, power procurement, construction, and hardware bring-up before accessing large-scale compute.\",\n   \"- e11 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5 2026-07-02] NVIDIA's offering includes token credits that let startups access compute resources without upfront capital outlays.\\n    Quote: Token credits are also part of the offering, giving startups a way to access compute resources without upfront capital outlays.\",\n   \"- e12 [fact; qz.com; original source NVIDIA; Sharon AI ; from gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5 2026-07-02] NVIDIA named Sharon AI as an initial partner, and Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: Nvidia named two initial partners. Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e4, e21, e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e13 [fact; qz.com; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5 2026-07-02] Firmus Technologies plans a campus in Batam, Indonesia, with capacity for up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs and 360 megawatts of power.\\n    Quote: A campus being developed by Firmus Technologies in Batam, Indonesia is planned at a capacity of up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs and 360 megawatts of power.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e5, e17, e28; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e14 [party_statement; qz.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:dde08c03c8dd6f66031632d5 2026-07-02] NVIDIA said AI demand is shifting from model development toward production inference workloads that require continuously operating infrastructure at scale.\\n    Quote: Nvidia framed the program as a response to a structural shift in AI demand, from model development toward production inference workloads that require continuously operating infrastructure at scale.\",\n   \"- e15 [fact; CNBC; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] NVIDIA said it was introducing a partnership program to connect AI startups with computing infrastructure from AI cloud service providers.\\n    Quote: Chipmaker Nvidia is expanding its support for fast-growing AI startups by introducing a partnership program that leverages its network of AI cloud service providers to offer these firms access to critical computing infrastructure, the company said Thursday.\",\n   \"- e16 [party_statement; CNBC; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Under the announced program, cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share product and cloud revenue with NVIDIA.\\n    Quote: Cloud-based AI firms, model builders and other enterprises will share both product and cloud revenue with Nvidia, which is positioning itself as an intermediary helping startups gain direct access to full-stack computing powered by Nvidia chips.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e9, e22; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e17 [party_statement; CNBC; original source Sharon AI and Firmus Technologies 2026-07-02; from gnews:d1364ee37c17c361ae74f563 2026-07-02] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 NVIDIA GPUs; Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam expected to reach 360 MW and house up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI will deploy up to 40,000 Nvidia GPUs, while AI infrastructure company Firmus Technologies says it is building a data center in Batam, Indonesia, which is expected to scale to 360 megawatts and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e13, e20, e24; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e22 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816 2026-07-02] NVIDIA announced a revenue-sharing and credit-support model intended to help startups access compute.\\n    Quote: In a blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress, the company pitched the “revenue-sharing and credit-support model” as a way to open compute access to startups that can’t finance it themselves.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e16; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e23 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source Sharon AI 2026-06-12; from gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816 2026-07-02] Sharon AI disclosed a six-year agreement covering 72 MW of new Australian data-center capacity, scaling to as many as 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: In an 8-K filing dated June 12th, Sharon AI disclosed that the agreement runs for six years and covers 72 MW of new Australian data center capacity built to Nvidia's DSX AI factory design, scaling to as many as 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e21; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e24 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816 2026-07-02] Firmus is building a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, Firmus is building a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, that’s expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e17; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e26 [fact; mitrade.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-07-02; from gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce 2026-07-02] NVIDIA announced an AI compute framework using revenue-sharing and credit-support agreements to help cloud providers deploy advanced hardware.\\n    Quote: NVIDIA’s new AI compute framework allows cloud providers to deploy advanced hardware using revenue-sharing and credit-support agreements.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e19; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e27 [fact; mitrade.com; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce 2026-07-02] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e12; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e28 [fact; mitrade.com; original source Firmus ; from gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce 2026-07-02] Firmus is developing an Indonesia campus that could support approximately 170,000 GPUs and 360 megawatts of power capacity.\\n    Quote: Firmus is developing a major campus in Indonesia that could support approximately 170,000 GPUs and 360 megawatts of power capacity.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e13; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e29 [third_party_view; SixSigmaCapital; original source SixSigmaCapital 2026-07-02; from gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce 2026-07-02] SixSigmaCapital said NVIDIA’s framework gives neoclouds greater certainty but less upside, and reduces NVIDIA’s reliance on hyperscalers.\\n    Quote: $NVDA Simplistically what this means for neoclouds,in my view, is it gives them certainty but takes away some of the upside. I think that’s a good deal for them.Also reduces $NVDA reliance on hyper scalers.\",\n   \"- e23 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source Sharon AI 2026-06-12; from gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816 2026-07-02] Sharon AI disclosed a six-year agreement covering 72 MW of new Australian data-center capacity, scaling to as many as 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: In an 8-K filing dated June 12th, Sharon AI disclosed that the agreement runs for six years and covers 72 MW of new Australian data center capacity built to Nvidia's DSX AI factory design, scaling to as many as 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e21, e34; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e24 [fact; Tom's Hardware; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:3854aeddaa3f31de00cf2816 2026-07-02] Firmus is building a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 NVIDIA GPUs.\\n    Quote: Meanwhile, Firmus is building a DSX-aligned campus in Batam, Indonesia, that’s expected to scale to 360 MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e17, e36; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e27 [fact; mitrade.com; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:bf158d067256a39f02f7c7ce 2026-07-02] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs.\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e12, e33; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e30 [party_statement; mlq.ai; original source Nvidia 2026-07-01; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Nvidia announced the AI Compute Partnership on July 1, 2026, to backstop neocloud customers' GPU deployments in return for a recurring share of cloud revenue generated by those GPUs.\\n    Quote: Nvidia on July 1 unveiled a new financing vehicle it calls the \\\"AI Compute Partnership,\\\" under which the chipmaker acts as a financial backstop for neocloud customers' GPU deployments and, in return, takes a recurring share of the cloud revenue those GPUs generate [1] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e1; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e31 [party_statement; mlq.ai; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Under Nvidia's AI Compute Partnership, Nvidia agrees to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate, backstopping lenders' exposure to neocloud deployments.\\n    Quote: The backstop mechanism works by Nvidia agreeing to rent back unused GPUs at a fixed rate, effectively de-risking lender exposure and making it easier for smaller cloud operators to secure capital for large GPU deployments [1] [3] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e18; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e32 [party_statement; mlq.ai; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Nvidia did not disclose the revenue-share percentage for the AI Compute Partnership and declined to provide details beyond its blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress.\\n    Quote: The revenue-share percentage was not disclosed; Nvidia declined to provide details beyond its blog post co-authored by CFO Colette Kress [3]\",\n   \"- e33 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Sharon AI and Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] The AI Compute Partnership's first adopters include Sharon AI, which plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, and Firmus Technologies, which is building a 360MW Batam campus targeting up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI (NASDAQ: SHAZ), an Australian sovereign-cloud provider planning up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, and Firmus Technologies, which is building a 360MW campus in Batam, Indonesia, targeting up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs [1] [2] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e27; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e34 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Sharon AI plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI, which listed on the Nasdaq in February 2026 via a $125 million IPO, is deploying up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs under a six-year agreement with Nvidia [2] [6] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e23; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e35 [fact; mlq.ai; original source Sharon AI ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Sharon AI raised $1.6 billion in a June 2026 private placement to fund its Nvidia-based AI factory.\\n    Quote: The company raised an additional $1.6 billion in private placement in June 2026 to fund its Nvidia-based AI factory\",\n   \"- e36 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] Firmus Technologies is constructing a Batam campus to Nvidia DGX SuperPOD (DSX) specifications, with plans for up to 360MW of capacity and up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Firmus Technologies, a private company, is constructing a campus in Batam, Indonesia, built to Nvidia's DGX SuperPOD (DSX) reference architecture specifications. The facility is expected to scale to 360MW and house up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs [1] [3] .\\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e24; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\",\n   \"- e33 [third_party_view; mlq.ai; original source Sharon AI and Firmus Technologies ; from gnews:9e0d5b0d6b3e603c60340128 2026-07-03] The AI Compute Partnership's first adopters include Sharon AI, which plans to deploy up to 40,000 Grace Blackwell GB300 GPUs, and Firmus Technologies, which is building a 360MW Batam campus targeting up to 170,000 Nvidia GPUs.\\n    Quote: Sharon AI (NASDAQ: SHAZ), an Australian sovereign-cloud provider planning up to 40,000 Grace Blackwel